# Do not commit generated code

When committing, **do not** `git add` or include generated trees. The human stages and commits those files.

**Generated (do not stage):**

- `frontend/bindings/**` — Wails TS bindings (`wails3 generate bindings` / `wails3 dev`)
- Any other Wails/codegen output (do not hand-edit either)

**Do:**

- Commit only source you wrote or edited (`internal/`, `frontend/src/`, tests, docs, etc.).
- If Go APIs changed, you may run bindings regen so the app builds locally — still **leave bindings unstaged**.
- After commit, mention leftover generated diffs so they can add them.

```bash
# ❌ BAD — staging bindings with the feature
git add frontend/bindings internal/service/file_service.go

# ✅ GOOD — source only
git add internal/service/file_service.go
# leave frontend/bindings/** unstaged
```
